# Trivy waiver ledger (req-cicd-security-scanning-4 / req-cicd-base-image-lifecycle-2).
#
# Every entry REQUIRES a reason comment directly above it: what the finding is,
# why it does not apply (or is accepted), who accepted it, and when. An entry
# without a reason is a review defect. This mirrors the FIPS waiver discipline
# (declare-vs-decide-vs-waive): the scanner reports, the OPERATOR waives —
# per-item, justified, in-repo where review sees it. Unfixed-upstream CVEs
# should generally NOT be listed here; they are visible-but-not-blocking by
# policy: the RELEASE gate (publish-release-tags.yml, tap#526) blocks a versioned tag
# only on High/Critical WITH a fix available, so an unfixable CVE stays visible without
# blocking every release. Entries here are read from the TAGGED commit, so a waiver
# written later never retroactively passes an older release.
#
# Format: one CVE/GHSA id per line, e.g.
#   # CVE-2026-XXXXX (libfoo): not reachable — TAP never invokes the vulnerable
#   #   codec path; accepted <name>, <date>. Revisit on libfoo bump.
#   CVE-2026-XXXXX
#
# CVE-2026-24049 (wheel 0.45.1, vendored inside setuptools/_vendor in the image
#   wheel-cache seed): malicious-wheel unpacking → ACE. Not reachable — wheel's
#   unpack routines are never invoked here: uv unpacks published wheels with its
#   own (Rust) implementation, and the vendored copy only runs inside setuptools
#   PEP 517 builds of first-party, tag-pinned plugin sources (building untrusted
#   source is already ACE by design, so the CVE adds no capability). Standalone
#   wheel is already floored >=0.46.2 (pyproject [tool.uv]
#   build-constraint-dependencies); the vendored copy is stuck because psycopg-c
#   3.3.4 hard-pins setuptools==80.3.1. Accepted George Chamales, 2026-08-11.
#   Revisit on psycopg-c bump.
CVE-2026-24049
# CVE-2026-59890 (setuptools 80.3.1, image wheel-cache seed): MANIFEST.in
#   exclusion bypass in sdist creation via Unicode normalization collision.
#   Producer-side packaging bug — relevant only when building sdists from trees
#   with attacker-chosen filenames; TAP's images never author sdists, and plugin
#   builds compile first-party, tag-pinned sources. setuptools>=83 floor is
#   unsatisfiable while psycopg-c 3.3.4 hard-pins setuptools==80.3.1 in
#   build-system.requires (pyproject [tool.uv] comment). Accepted George
#   Chamales, 2026-08-11. Revisit on psycopg-c bump.
CVE-2026-59890
# CVE-2026-23949 (jaraco.context 5.3.0, vendored inside setuptools/_vendor in
#   the image wheel-cache seed): path traversal in the tarball() extraction
#   helper. Not reachable — nothing in TAP imports jaraco.context; it is present
#   only as setuptools vendored code, and setuptools' build/install flow does not
#   feed tar archives through that helper. Fixed only via setuptools>=83, blocked
#   by the same psycopg-c setuptools==80.3.1 hard pin. Accepted George Chamales,
#   2026-08-11. Revisit on psycopg-c bump.
CVE-2026-23949
